Part V — Advanced topics: deadlock reasoning (4 marks). Fill the missing concepts.
```java
// Bad idea: different methods acquire the same two locks in different orders.
// Thread 1: acquire A, then acquire B.
// Thread 2: acquire B, then acquire A.
```
This can cause {bug}. A common fix is to impose one global lock-acquisition {rule}. This breaks the Coffman condition called {condition}. The kind of correctness property violated is mainly {property}.
